{"Title":"An Act relative to dangerous high speed pursuits","BillNumber":"H3281","DocketNumber":"HD2783","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"DRC1","Name":"Daniel R. Carey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DRC1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:24:42.05"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"DRC1","Name":"Daniel R. Carey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DRC1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:24:42.05"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3281/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Carey of Easthampton, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3281) of Daniel R. Carey relative to dangerous high-speed pursuits.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 90 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 25 the following section 25A:-\r\n\tAny person who, while operating or in charge of a motor vehicle, shall refuse to stop when signaled to stop by any police officer who is in uniform or who displays his badge conspicuously on the outside of his outer coat or garment, and who after said refusal operates the motor vehicle negligently or recklessly upon any way or in any place to which the public has a right of access, or any place to which members of the public have access as invitees or licensees, so that the lives or safety of the public might be endangered, and who does so with the intent to evade or elude any police officer or otherwise avoid apprehension, shall be punished by imprisonment in the state prison for not more than five years, or by imprisonment in a jail or house of correction for not more than two and one half years, or by a fine of not more than $2,500.00, or by both such fine and imprisonment.\r\n\tThere shall be an assessment of $250 against a person who is convicted of, is placed on probation for, or is granted a continuance without a finding for or otherwise pleads guilty to or admits to a finding of sufficient facts of operating a motor vehicle in violation of this section. The amount collected pursuant to this assessment shall be deposited monthly by the court with the state treasurer for who shall deposit it into the Head Injury Treatment Services Trust Fund. The assessment shall not be subject to reduction or waiver by the court for any reason.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}